{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_016E5vGvu5CXS4MMuJGeTWuJ", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"memories\":[{\"confidence\":0.8,\"content\":\"Tax rules came out of a review with the finance team in March 2026 after customers reported invoices that were off by a cent. Tax amounts use banker's rounding (decimal.ROUND_HALF_EVEN), never ROUND_HALF_UP. Round the tax of each line item separately, per line, and then sum the rounded line taxes; never round the invoice total.\",\"criticality\":0.5,\"epistemic\":\"decision\",\"id\":\"01a0f7dd-aba2-7e41-9574-84f99ee057e1\",\"logical\":[],\"physical\":[\"src/billing/tax.py\"],\"provenance\":\"human\",\"score\":0.7831239832213148,\"score_breakdown\":{\"criticality\":0.5,\"decay\":0.0,\"final_score\":0.7831239832213148,\"keyword\":0.9750600661427731,\"relevance\":0.5,\"rerank\":1.3785202503204346,\"scope\":0.0,\"scope_multiplier\":1.0,\"semantic\":0.6790589862010976,\"situation_multiplier\":1.0,\"trust\":1.0,\"trust_multiplier\":1.0},\"status\":\"active\",\"summary\":\"Tax rounding rule\",\"tags\":[\"billing\",\"tax\"],\"type\":\"decision\",\"visibility\":\"shared\"},{\"confidence\":0.8,\"content\":\"Billing code moves amounts between invoices, refunds, tax and the ledger, and every one of those paths has been bitten by rounding drift in the past. The rule that came out of that: store and pass every monetary amount as integer cents using the Money type in src/billing/money.py. Never use float for money, not even for intermediate math. New fields that hold an amount end in _cents, for example discount_cents.\",\"criticality\":0.5,\"epistemic\":\"fact\",\"id\":\"01a0f7dd-8418-7db0-b525-586a666e2772\",\"logical\":[],\"physical\":[\"src/billing/\"],\"provenance\":\"human\",\"score\":0.3330553313183382,\"score_breakdown\":{\"criticality\":0.5,\"decay\":0.0,\"final_score\":0.3330553313183382,\"keyword\":0.059800620432964566,\"relevance\":0.5,\"rerank\":-0.652671